// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR E_TYPE_NOT_IN_SET
//
// Registry #941, the STATIC-METHOD form in argument position — the second door the
// row named as open, now closed.
//
// `only_ints(Box.new())` compiled clean while the same value through a binding was
// refused. `Box.new()` parses as `Call { func: Path(["Box","new"]) }` — the parser
// recognises a known type name and emits `Path`, not `Member` — so `call_return_ty`'s
// `Ident` branch never saw it and the D310 membership check silently did not run.
//
// TWO FALSE POSITIVES ON THE WAY HERE, both caught by the corpus and both worth
// naming, because each one narrowed the fix:
//
//   1. A constructor declared `-> Self` returned the literal `Self`, so the bound
//      check asked whether `Self` satisfies `Src` and said no —
//      `p176repro_result_valuerecord_err.nv:53` on perfectly legal code. `Self` on a
//      static means the receiving type; it is substituted now, and a `Self` nested
//      inside a compound return (`Result[Self, E]`) answers `None` rather than
//      guessing.
//   2. Substituting the bare name dropped the type's parameters: `BufWriter.new(...)`
//      on `BufWriter[W]` produced `BufWriter`, and
//      `std/src/io/wrapper_ctor_inference_test.nv:21` failed with
//      `[E_RECV_SHAPE_MISMATCH] requires receiver shape `BufWriter[W]`, got
//      `BufWriter``. Answering with a name minus its parameters trades one wrong
//      answer for another, so the arm now takes NON-GENERIC types only — the same
//      guard the constructor branch beside it already carried.
//
// STILL OPEN in #941, and this fixture does not touch it: the RECEIVER half
// (`Meters(2.5).try_to_i16()` builds and prints `true`) and the generic-static form
// (`only_ints(Vec[int].of(1))` is still accepted, measured). Both are named in the
// row and in `scripts/guards/fixed-but-open.baseline`.
//
// Spec: D310 (`spec/decisions/02-types.md`, "Type-set bounds").
module neg.p941_static_arg_bound_neg

type P941Box priv { n int }

fn P941Box.new() -> P941Box => { n: 1 }

fn only_ints[T Ints](x T) -> int => 0

fn pass_a_static_call_straight_into_a_bounded_parameter() Io -> () {
    // nova:expect E_TYPE_NOT_IN_SET -- `P941Box` is not a member of `Ints`; the constructor spelling used to skip the check entirely
    println(only_ints(P941Box.new()))
}
